name: "High-throughput exploration of 984 Suzuki-Miyaura and Buchwald-Hartwig couplings for the C6-functionalization of 1H-indazol-3-amines"
description: "A full-factorial dataset of 984 Suzuki-Miyaura cross-couplings and Buchwald-Hartwig aminations investigating the C6-functionalization of 1H-indazol-3-amines. The reactions were studied in a high-throughput experimentation (HTE) campaign to map the reaction condition space for the optimization of bioisosteric scaffolds in early-stage fragment-based drug discovery. The screen evaluated 41 distinct coupling partners (20 boronic acids/esters, 21 amines) against 24 reaction conditions, permuting 6 catalysts, 2 bases, and 2 solvents. Reaction outcomes were determined by LC-MS relative product formation. Reactions were performed by the Koch group at the University of Münster, and the publication is available at [DOI to be added]. Important Note: For the Buchwald-Hartwig series, reactions targeting putative products 28 and 31 showed the correct mass by LC-MS, but subsequent NMR characterization of the isolated material did not match the assigned structure; these have been flagged in the dataset as unidentified products, and a reaction identifier has been added to subset the dataset by the result of the NMR structure confirmation."
reactions {
  identifiers {
    type: REACTION_TYPE
    value: "Buchwald-Hartwig coupling"
  }
  identifiers {
    type: CUSTOM
    details: "dataset subset for confirmed versus ambiguous product determination"
    value: "confirmed product determination"
  }
  inputs {
    key: "Base"
